In mixed cropping, two or more than two crops seeds are mixed randomly and broadcast everywhere without any distinct row arrangement. But in intercropping, there is a crop, and in the middle of those crops, some crops are sown in a distinct ratio such as 2:1. It is only between the rows but not all around the crop. Single crop monoculture is easy, but cover crop or a border crop or a barrier or a trap context is done when around a main crop, another crop's boundary is grown so that the main crop remains safe.

